The Classic ELB came up, so the block only covers the newer NLB/ALB load balancers. I've also fixed the two routing problems in the code. Nothing is deployed yet: the new frontend image hasn't been built, and none of these changes have been applied to the cluster.

What I changed:

backend-ingress.yml: it now holds two Ingresses.
app-ingress sends / to the frontend.
api-ingress sends /api/... to the backend and removes the /api prefix, so /api/ reaches the backend as /. That matches the routes in index.ts, so the backend code and image don't need to change.
They're separate because the prefix rewrite would apply to every path in one Ingress.
App.tsx: both requests now go to /api/ instead of the old k8s-2 load balancer address. The frontend and the API now share one address (the ELB), so the requests go through the ingress.
nginx-controller.sh: I added the annotate command, so a fresh setup gets a Classic ELB again.
Run these to deploy:


cd ..\frontend
docker build -t devsoumya7/frontend:latest .
docker push devsoumya7/frontend:latest
cd ..\k8s-3-ingess-controller
kubectl apply -f backend-ingress.yml
kubectl rollout restart deployment frontend-dep
The frontend deployment uses the latest tag and always pulls the image, so the restart picks up the new build.

